    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey i need some help troubleshooting a sublimation issue. we've been running heat transfers for polyester blends but the color vibrancy is way lower than it should be and the edges look blurry. we are currently at 200c for 40 seconds with 4 bar of pressure. any idea what might be causing the poor transfer or the bleeding around the edges?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The low vibrancy and blurry edges on polyester blends are likely caused by improper heat settings where the polymer isn't fusing correctly with the ink. Since your current settings are an inch below the typical 220°C–240°C range recommended for polyester, try increasing the temperature to 230°C and extending the time to 50–60 seconds while maintaining 5–7 psi for better adhesion. Additionally, clean the roller wipes and check that your pigment ink is compatible with the sublimation film; poor quality granules or worn transfers can also cause bleeding.",
      "source": "target",
