      "content": "yeah we definitely use sublimation ink so it's not that. we also checked the humidity and it's pretty controlled in the plant. the thing is, the patterns are inconsistent. sometimes a part of the design looks perfect, and then a few inches away, the ink just seems to have \"vanished\" or faded out completely, even though the heat and pressure were identical. it's like the pigment is being sabotaged or something. do you think there's any way the ink could be dropping out of the transfer during the heat cycle?",
